# Another program's canvas may repeat a card's id. The canvas owner gives the second card a
# place of its own, and the whiteboard opens at it: Enter on a task of the second card, in the
# agenda, selects that card and not the first one (the status line names the selected card's
# size). An edit then changes the second card. tests/drive.rs writes Inbox/Twins.canvas and
# reads it after: the first card and both ids as they were.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
env COLD_LAVA_TODAY=2026-11-07
wait-for example-workspace
keys A
wait-for ↑↓ move · x tick · ⏎ open
keys /
type feed the twin
wait-for / feed the twin▏
keys enter
wait-for 1 of 16 rows · /feed the twin
keys j enter
wait-for whiteboard Twins · 2 cards
wait-for text card  320×120
screen
keys enter
wait-for editing · type text · ⏎ new line · Esc done (saves)
type , twice
wait-for Feed the twin, twice▏
keys esc
wait-gone editing · type text
expect text card  320×120
screen
keys q
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
keys q
exits 0
